Asha, Rohan, and Priya are in my flat.
We all stand near the open balcony doors.
Everyone has cups of hot chai in their hands.
Outside, the wind is blowing extremely fast.
The wind is driving the rain horizontally.
But we are safe just inside.
We stay completely dry.
We watch this fierce rain in awe.
I tell them, "I like this intense weather very much."
Last week, only gentle rain fell.
But today, very intense rain has come.
Rohan laughs and points at the water.
He says, "Look, how fierce the rain is today!"
Priya says, "Yes, Mumbai's rain is very special."
Asha drinks her chai and says, "This hot chai is also very good."
I look at my friends.
I came to Mumbai for a job.
But now, I have found good friends here.
With friends, I really love this kind of rain.
Together, we enjoy the downpour.
